.TH CHTTPSVR_IS_RUNNING 3 "2026-10-13" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_is_running \- report whether a server listens
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_is_running(chttpsvr srv, bool *running_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Stores in *running_out whether srv listens.  A server listens from
the moment a successful chttpsvr_start returns until its stop begins,
whether that stop comes from chttpsvr_stop, chttpsvr_engine_stop or
chttpsvr_destroy.  A server that was never started, one whose start
failed, and one that is in the middle of a start or a stop do not
listen.

The answer is a snapshot, and another thread can start or stop the
server right after the call returns.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
srv           The server handle.
running_out   Receives true when the server listens and false
              otherwise.  It receives false on every failure.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       *running_out holds the answer.
ccol_invalid_args  srv is CHTTPSVR_NULL or a stale handle, or
                   running_out is NULL.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call from any thread, including a handler or a middleware of
srv, while a start or a stop of srv runs.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bool running = false;
if (chttpsvr_is_running(srv, &running) == ccol_success && !running)
  chttpsvr_start(srv, &cfg);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_start (3),
.BR chttpsvr_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_bound_port (3),
.BR chttpsvr_bound_address (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_stop (3)
